# Supercronic crontab, run alongside uvicorn in the same Fly machine (see the
# Dockerfile CMD). Supercronic runs each entry through /bin/sh with the
# container's own environment, so Fly secrets and fly.toml's [env] DATABASE_URL
# are already in scope. Times are UTC -- Fly machines have no local timezone.
#
# TWO ENTRIES, NOT ONE CHAINED WITH `&&`. They are independent jobs and the
# recheck is the more valuable of the two (a live pass found 20 of the 60 oldest
# tracked listings already dead). Chained, a transient board-API failure in the
# observation pass -- which exits non-zero on `ok: false` -- would silently skip
# the recheck for that day too.
#
# DAILY IS A FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENT for the observation pass, not tidiness:
# full_auto.EVERGREEN_SEEN_DENSITY divides days-seen by days-since-discovery, so
# a missed day inflates the denominator while the numerator stands still. Gaps
# suppress the signal rather than delaying it. Check `--status` weekly; a crawl
# that has stopped looks healthy in every field except distinct_observation_days.
#
# Absolute paths on purpose: these must not depend on supercronic having
# inherited /app as its working directory.
0 3 * * * cd /app && python scripts/observe_listings.py
30 3 * * * cd /app && python scripts/recheck_liveness.py
